WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.280
Stone Age emotions. Medieval institutions. Godlike technology.

2
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:13.720
This is not a bug. It's the operating system. And the operating system is trying to kill you with cheeseburgers and nuclear

3
00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:21.720
weapons simultaneously. The Selfish Gene Made You Illogical (It Was a Good Idea at the Time).

4
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:31.520
Richard Dawkins put it perfectly: "We are survival machines, robot vehicles blindly programmed to preserve the selfish molecules

5
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:40.280
known as genes.". Translation: You're a meat puppet controlled by chemicals whose entire business plan is "make more chemicals

6
00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:45.120
before something eats us.". Your genes don't care if you're happy.

7
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:53.980
They don't care if you live past thirty. They care about exactly one thing: making copies of themselves before something

8
00:00:53.980 --> 00:01:00.980
with teeth finds you. For ninety-nine point nine percent of human history, this was brilliant engineering.

9
00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:09.640
Now it's why you eat an entire pizza at midnight, feel anxious about emails, fund nuclear weapons capable of ending all

10
00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:13.420
life, and slowly develop diabetes while your teeth fall out.

11
00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:22.760
The genes are still celebrating. You are not. Part 1: Your Brain Was Optimized for a World That Doesn't Exist.

12
00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:33.360
The Scarcity Brain (Or: Why It's Hard to Stop Eating). For two hundred thousand years, calories were rare.

13
00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:38.040
Finding a beehive full of honey wasn't "prediabetes in a tree."

14
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:43.380
It was the difference between your children surviving winter or not existing anymore.

15
00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:52.860
So evolution programmed you with one simple rule: When you find calories, eat ALL of them RIGHT NOW before the hyenas show

16
00:01:52.860 --> 00:02:00.980
up. Fast forward to today: You live within walking distance of fourteen restaurants selling three thousand eight hundred

17
00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:05.040
calorie meals. Each meal contains twice your daily calorie needs.

18
00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:10.960
Your ancient brain still screams: "EAT EVERYTHING! WINTER IS COMING!".

19
00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:20.480
Winter never comes. Diabetes often does. The exact same brain that kept your ancestors alive by gorging on mammoth fat is

20
00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:25.460
now killing you with McDonald's. Evolution doesn't do software updates.

21
00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:33.380
You're running two hundred thousand year old code on hardware that was designed for an environment that no longer exists.

22
00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:41.700
It's like running a nuclear power plant on Windows Ninety-Five, except the nuclear power plant is your civilization and

23
00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:49.260
it's connected to the internet. The Violence Module (Or: Why You Tend to Prefer Bombs Over Band-Aids).

24
00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:53.980
Fifteen to thirty percent of your ancestors died from violence.

25
00:02:54.700 --> 00:03:02.920
Not disease. Not starvation. Other humans, smashing their heads with rocks over territorial disputes about berry bushes.

26
00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:10.250
You've since upgraded the rocks to intercontinental ballistic missiles, but the berry bush energy remains.

27
00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:15.000
The tribes that survived weren't the peaceful, loving ones.

28
00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:23.040
They were the paranoid, survival-focused ones who: Assumed every stranger might want to kill them (often statistically accurate).

29
00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:30.800
Struck first when threatened (natural selection at work). Formed tight combat groups to kill other groups (teamwork!).

30
00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:35.420
Hoarded weapons obsessively (can never have too many pointy sticks).

31
00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:45.380
Your brain is still running this exact software. That's why: Humanity spends two point seven two trillion dollars annually

32
00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:52.240
on weapons you'll probably never use. You instinctively distrust people who don't look like your tribe.

33
00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:57.840
Twitter arguments feel like actual combat (your amygdala can't tell the difference).

34
00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:03.340
Countries with ten thousand nuclear weapons are worried they don't have enough.

35
00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:08.120
The violence module kept your ancestors from getting clubbed to death.

36
00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:12.900
Now it's building weapons that could end all life on Earth.

37
00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:17.820
Computer scientists call this "feature creep." Biologists call it "maladaptive."

38
00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:26.180
I call it "the reason I'm writing this book.". The Tribal Brain: Why Democracy is Struggling.

39
00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:33.860
Dunbar's number says humans can maintain stable relationships with about one hundred and fifty people.

40
00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:42.620
That's your entire social capacity. Your brain has one hundred and fifty slots for caring about people, and you've filled

41
00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:48.780
most of them with coworkers you tolerate and celebrities who don't know you exist.

42
00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:55.980
For two hundred thousand years, this worked great: Your tribe had one hundred and fifty people.

43
00:04:56.460 --> 00:05:01.220
You knew everyone personally. Decisions affected people you could see.

44
00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:09.980
Free riders got kicked out or starved. Now you live in a democracy with three hundred and thirty-five million strangers

45
00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:16.580
where: You vote for people you've never met. To make decisions about people you'll never see.

46
00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:23.100
Using tax money that feels imaginary. To solve problems your brain struggles to comprehend.

47
00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:31.000
Your brain treats anything outside your one hundred and fifty-person monkeysphere as an abstraction.

48
00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:39.820
That's why: You care more about your neighbor's barking dog than ten thousand people dying of malaria (the dog is RIGHT

49
00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:44.660
THERE being loud, malaria is just a concept with numbers attached).

50
00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:53.320
Local corruption makes you angrier than trillion-dollar Pentagon waste (the local guy stole ten thousand dollars you can

51
00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:59.110
imagine, the Pentagon lost two point five trillion dollars which is just syllables).

52
00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:09.540
You'll donate to save one sick child but ignore statistics about millions (one child has a face, millions is just a very

53
00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:18.080
big number that makes your brain hurt). Democracy feels broken (because it requires a level of empathy your monkey brain

54
00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:25.340
literally cannot produce). Part 2: Genetic Slavery is Literally Killing Us.

55
00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:31.860
We're Dying from Winning. Evolution prepared you for scarcity, predators, and violence.

56
00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:40.960
You got abundance, safety, and Netflix. Your bodies responded with the biological equivalent of a computer trying to print

57
00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:50.500
a sandwich: Evolution prepared us for starvation, we got unlimited calories, and the result is a forty-two point four percent

58
00:06:50.860 --> 00:07:00.310
obesity rate. Evolution prepared us for constant physical threats, we got office chairs, and the result is anxiety disorders.

59
00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:09.240
Evolution prepared us for a thirty-year lifespan, we got an eighty-year lifespan, and the result is bodies that fall apart

60
00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:19.360
at forty. Evolution prepared us for small tribes, we got global society, and the result is constant existential dread.

61
00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:26.060
Evolution prepared us for clear immediate dangers, we got abstract future risks, and the result is difficulty planning.

62
00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:28.800
Evolution prepared us for scarce mates, we got dating apps, and the result is paralysis from too much choice.

63
00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:34.340
Your genes succeeded spectacularly. Eight billion copies and counting.

64
00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:39.070
From evolution's perspective, this is an unqualified triumph.

65
00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:47.340
You're just the disposable meat robot they used to do it. Now you're confused why you can't stop eating Cheetos at two A.M.

66
00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:57.060
Living in the Most Irrational Timeline. Here's the cosmic joke: Humanity has never been safer, healthier, or more prosperous.

67
00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:00.580
You've also never been closer to accidentally ending everything.

68
00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:05.400
You solved poverty and invented nuclear war in the same century.

69
00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:13.120
Very on-brand. You solved all the hard problems. Then you immediately invented worse ones to replace them.

70
00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:16.520
Like winning the lottery and using the money to buy a tiger.

71
00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:23.840
Problems you solved. Starvation (you throw away forty percent of food because storing it is inconvenient).

72
00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:30.450
Predators (you murdered them into extinction, then put them in zoos so your children could see what you killed).

73
00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:38.520
Infant mortality (basically eradicated in developed countries, which makes the death rate in poor countries feel more optional

74
00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:44.920
and thus more tragic). Most infectious diseases (vaccines work despite what Facebook says).

75
00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:52.940
Dying at thirty (now you complain about turning forty, which your ancestors would consider a miracle worth celebrating daily).

76
00:08:54.040 --> 00:09:01.840
New problems you invented with your big brains: Nuclear weapons (enough to end civilization twenty times because once wasn't

77
00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:07.280
enough). Climate change (you're terraforming your only planet by accident).

78
00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:15.160
Antibiotic resistance (ten million deaths annually by twenty-fifty because you gave antibiotics to cows).

79
00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:20.660
A.I. that might become sentient and decide you're the problem (the A.I.

80
00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:27.180
would be correct). Social media (voluntary psychological torture you pay for with attention).

81
00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:35.400
Humanity is a toddler who found the nuclear launch codes. Godlike technological power, hamster-level impulse control.

82
00:09:36.520 --> 00:09:40.960
On most planets, civilizations develop wisdom before weapons.

83
00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:47.790
Yours did the opposite and seems quite pleased about it. Part 3: Why You Can't Just "Be Better".

84
00:09:48.340 --> 00:09:52.160
Your conscious mind controls maybe five percent of your decisions.

85
00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:58.260
The other ninety-five percent is your ancient lizard brain running software older than agriculture.

86
00:09:58.840 --> 00:10:04.640
You think you're the pilot. You're actually a passenger who occasionally gets to suggest a direction.

87
00:10:05.140 --> 00:10:10.080
This scales to civilization. The fear of violent death is older than language.

88
00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:16.440
The fear of slow death from disease? Your brain files that under "boring, deal with later."

89
00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:24.820
Later never comes. Neither does the cure. That's why you spent two point seven two trillion dollars on weapons while cancer

90
00:10:24.820 --> 00:10:30.090
research got pocket change. Part 4: The Prison We Built Ourselves.

91
00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:38.840
You Vote for Monkeys in Human-Skin Suits. Democracy asks your stone-age brain to make civilization-level decisions.

92
00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:43.060
It goes exactly as well as asking a labrador retriever to do your taxes.

93
00:10:44.020 --> 00:10:50.620
You vote based on: Who looks stronger (alpha male bias - your brain thinks the election is a wrestling match).

94
00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:55.290
Who your tribe likes (social proof - if the clan approves, must be good).

95
00:10:55.740 --> 00:11:00.300
Who makes you feel safe (fear sells better than policy ever will).

96
00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:06.680
Who you'd have a beer with (relevance: zero, but your brain insists this matters for nuclear policy decisions).

97
00:11:07.780 --> 00:11:12.740
You don't vote based on: Complex policy analysis (too many words, brain hurts).

98
00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:17.080
Long-term thinking (your brain stops caring after next winter).

99
00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:21.620
Statistical reality (numbers are abstract, feelings are real).

100
00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:30.020
Actual competence (boring, where's the tribal signaling?). You elect leaders using the same brain circuits your ancestors

101
00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:36.540
used to pick the guy with the biggest club. The Military-Industrial Cortex.

102
00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:40.960
Your brain's fear center (amygdala) is directly connected to your voting finger.

103
00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:50.560
Politicians know this. Say "terrorism" and your lizard brain overrides everything: More people die from falling out of bed

104
00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:55.320
than terrorism. You're one thousand times more likely to die from heart disease.

105
00:11:56.080 --> 00:12:04.400
But terrorism *feels* scarier, because evolution optimized your fear response for things with faces, not things with cholesterol.

106
00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:12.100
So you spend trillions on defense against threats that barely register statistically, while the diseases actually killing

107
00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:20.200
you get a fraction of the budget. Your bed is more dangerous than Al-Qaeda, but nobody's declared a War on Furniture.

108
00:12:21.480 --> 00:12:26.520
Part 5: Breaking the Chains. Every single one of you is going to die.

109
00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:34.340
From the most powerful president to the lowliest pauper, you face a life of gradually escalating suffering until it ends.

110
00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:41.820
This is not a warning. It's a weather report. But now? You live in a world of abundance and nuclear weapons.

111
00:12:42.580 --> 00:12:47.800
You can feed everyone twice over, but you'd rather burn grain to keep prices high.

112
00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:56.480
You can cure diseases, but you'd rather sell treatments forever (cured customers don't come back; bad for quarterly earnings).

113
00:12:57.360 --> 00:13:04.760
The software running human civilization is ten thousand years out of date, and the bugs are literally killing you.

114
00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:09.940
Why don't you update the software? You could be immortal space wizards.

115
00:13:10.460 --> 00:13:18.020
Instead you're cave-dwelling murderers with better tools. Because the current system makes irrationality profitable.

116
00:13:18.780 --> 00:13:25.040
Spectacularly profitable. Every bomb makes someone rich. Every missile funds a yacht.

117
00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:30.500
Every war creates a billionaire. Disease is profitable too.

118
00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:38.520
Not curing it, treating it. Insulin costs three hundred dollars a vial because dead diabetics don't buy insulin.

119
00:13:38.860 --> 00:13:43.100
But cured diabetics don't either. So you keep them barely alive.

120
00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:48.640
It's good business. The people making money from war and disease aren't evil.

121
00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:53.320
They're just rational actors in a system that rewards the wrong things.

122
00:13:53.820 --> 00:14:00.540
You can't change human nature. Two hundred thousand years of evolution doesn't care about your TED talk.

123
00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:07.200
But you can create economic systems that make curing people more profitable than killing them.

124
00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:11.240
That's the only upgrade your species has ever responded to.

125
00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:16.970
Part 6: Breaking Free from Your Programming. You're not broken.

126
00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:23.920
You're just running 200,000-year-old software on hardware that was designed for a completely different world.

127
00:14:24.560 --> 00:14:31.360
Your brain evolved to live 30 years, feed 5 people, avoid tigers, and fight neighboring tribes.

128
00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:39.740
Expecting it to handle nuclear policy, climate change, and a 24-hour news cycle is like expecting a calculator to run a

129
00:14:39.740 --> 00:14:45.640
space program. The calculator isn't broken. You're just asking it to do something it was never built for.

130
00:14:46.340 --> 00:14:51.400
You can't fight 200,000 years of evolution. But you can hack it.

131
00:14:51.940 --> 00:15:00.520
That's what a one percent treaty does. Instead of asking people to be rational (impossible), use their irrational impulses:

132
00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:04.480
Greed: Make curing disease more profitable than building bombs.

133
00:15:05.100 --> 00:15:08.820
Fear: Make politicians more scared of voters than lobbyists.

134
00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:14.440
Tribalism: Create an us-versus-disease tribe instead of us-versus-them.

135
00:15:15.300 --> 00:15:19.920
Social proof: Get three point five percent participation so others follow.

136
00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:30.340
Immediate rewards: Pay people cash to join medical trials. Your genes enslaved you in brains that want sugar, fear strangers,

137
00:15:30.460 --> 00:15:35.880
and cannot comprehend statistics. But they also gave you the ability to see the prison.

138
00:15:36.440 --> 00:15:40.420
No other animal can think: "Wow, my instincts are completely illogical."

139
00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:46.940
That's uniquely human. Use it. A one percent treaty doesn't ask you to be better.

140
00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:52.020
It assumes you won't be, and redirects your worst impulses toward not dying.

141
00:15:52.400 --> 00:15:57.980
It's the only plan that works for the species you actually are, rather than the species you wish you were.
